<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7233" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάπλοος</span></b> , 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναπλήρ-πλους</span></b> , ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναπλέω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sailing up-stream,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.4
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἀ. ἐκ τῆς θαλάττης,</span>
			of a <i>canal</i> from the sea to an inland harbour, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Criti.</u>
				115d
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				117e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>putting out</i> to sea, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.53.13
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>sailing back, return,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				4.7.3
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				1.3.15
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>